{"batchcomplete":"","query":{"normalized":[{"from":"Old_Coin","to":"Old Coin"},{"from":"Mummified_Hand","to":"Mummified Hand"},{"from":"Busted_Crown","to":"Busted Crown"},{"from":"Paper_Phrog","to":"Paper Phrog"},{"from":"Sacred_Bark","to":"Sacred Bark"},{"from":"Medical_Kit","to":"Medical Kit"},{"from":"Question_Card","to":"Question Card"},{"from":"Ancient_Tea_Set","to":"Ancient Tea Set"},{"from":"Lizard_Tail","to":"Lizard Tail"},{"from":"Molten_Egg","to":"Molten Egg"},{"from":"Cracked_Core","to":"Cracked Core"},{"from":"Symbiotic_Virus","to":"Symbiotic Virus"},{"from":"Letter_Opener","to":"Letter Opener"}],"pages":{"1942":{"pageid":1942,"ns":0,"title":"Ancient Tea Set","revisions":[{"revid":56320,"parentid":56319,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Rename|Ancient Tea Set|Venerable Tea Set}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n| Name        = Ancient Tea Set\n| Image       = AncientTeaSet.png\n| Rarity      = Common\n| Description = Whenever you enter a Rest Site, start the next combat with 2 extra {{KW|Energy}}.\n| Flavor      = The key to a refreshing night's rest.\n| GivesToPlayer = Energy\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Energy}}\n{{R|Ancient Tea Set}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Common|Common}} [[Relic]].\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], by buying from the [[Merchant]], or found in a [[Small Chest]] or [[Medium Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Calling Bell}}, {{R|Shovel}}, {{R|Black Star}}, and {{R|Matryoshka}}.\n** {{R|Calling Bell}}'s {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Common|Common}} relic can be {{R|Ancient Tea Set}}.\n** {{R|Matryoshka}}'s extra relic has a 75% chance of being {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Common|Common}}, which can be {{R|Ancient Tea Set}}.\n* Can be obtained from the following [[Events]]:\n** {{E|We Meet Again!}}: Can give {{R|Ancient Tea Set}} in exchange for either a [[Potion]], some [[Gold]], or a [[Card]].\n** {{E|Wheel of Change}}: Can drop {{R|Ancient Tea Set}} as a prize.\n** {{E|Big Fish}}: Can give {{R|Ancient Tea Set}} along with {{C|Regret}}.\n** {{E|Dead Adventurer}}: Either by choosing {{Frame|Search}} and getting {{R|Ancient Tea Set}} as a reward, or by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|Ancient Tea Set}}).\n** {{E|Scrap Ooze}}: Can give {{R|Ancient Tea Set}} with an X% chance, for increasing amounts of damage and likelihood of success on repeated attempts.\n** {{E|Pleading Vagrant}}: Can give {{R|Ancient Tea Set}} in exchange for either 85 [[Gold]] by choosing {{Frame|Offer Gold}}, or {{C|Shame}} by choosing {{Frame|Rob}}.\n** {{E|The Mausoleum}}: Can give {{R|Ancient Tea Set}} along with {{C|Writhe}}.\n\n== Spawn Restrictions ==\nCan only be obtained below floor 49 (the last [[Rest Site]] before the [[Bosses#Act_3_Bosses|Act 3 Boss]]).\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n==== Synergies ====\n* Works automatically after any [[Map Locations#Rest Sites|Rest Site]], regardless of whether you rest or smith.\n* The extra energy can help to play {{KW|Innate}} cards (or cards added to the opening hand using {{R|Bottled Flame}}, {{R|Bottled Lightning}}, and {{R|Bottled Tornado}}) more easily.\n* The extra energy can be more easily used with the additional card draw on turn 1 from {{R|Bag of Preparation}}, {{R|Ring of the Snake}}, and {{R|Snecko Eye}}.\n* {{C|Whirlwind}}, {{C|Skewer}}, and other X-cost cards benefit greatly from the extra energy.\n* {{R|Ice Cream}} can preserve unused energy from the bonus for later turns.\n\n==== Neutral ====\n* Since there is always a [[Map Locations#Rest Sites|Rest Site]] before a [[Boss]] (except in Act 4), the extra energy can help set up for these difficult fights.\n* The effect does ''not'' stack multiple times if multiple [[Map Locations#Rest Sites|Rest Sites]] are visited before entering combat.\n\n==== Negative ====\n* Provides no direct benefit during longer fights if the bonus energy is not capitalized on immediately.\n* Routing around Rest Sites to maximize event/elite rooms reduces its usefulness.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 52: Release Date Price Increase'''\n** Updated relic asset for Ancient Tea Set.\n* '''Weekly Patch 8: Ooh Shiny!'''\n** Wording: Consistency in description for Ancient Tea Set and Eternal Feather.\n* '''Weekly Patch 4: Full speed ahead!'''\n** Fixing typos for Ancient Tea Set's flavor description.\n* '''Weekly Patch 3: Balance Balance Balance'''\n** Ancient Tea Set now properly saves its state, continuing won't remove it.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"3077":{"pageid":3077,"ns":0,"title":"Busted Crown","revisions":[{"revid":56922,"parentid":50916,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Busted Crown\n|Image       = BustedCrown.png\n|Rarity      = Boss\n|Description = Gain 1 {{KW|Energy}} at the start of your turn. Future card rewards have 2 less cards to choose from.\n|Flavor      = The Champ's crown... or a pale imitation?\n|GivesToPlayer = Energy\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Energy}}\n{{R|Busted Crown}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Boss|Boss}} [[Relic]].\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be obtained from [[Boss Swap]].\n* After fighting a [[Boss]], {{R|Busted Crown}} can be offered as a choice of 3 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Boss|Boss Relics}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\nOnly card rewards that would permanently add a card to the player's deck are affected by {{R|Busted Crown}}. Effects will generally mention ''\"obtain a card\"'' or specifically adding a card ''\"to your deck\"'' when they acts as card rewards, while effects that '''don't''' act as card rewards will always be phrased like ''\"choose 1 of 3 cards\"'' while in combat.\n\nFor completeness, all scenarios that seem like they could be considered a card reward during normal gameplay are listed in the sections below depending on whether they are affected by {{R|Busted Crown}} or not.\n\n=== Affected Card Rewards ===\n\nThe following card reward screens are affected by {{R|Busted Crown}} and will show 2 fewer cards to choose from:\n\n* End-of-combat card rewards from defeating [[Monsters|normal enemies]].\n* End-of-combat card rewards from defeating [[Elites|elites]].\n* The guaranteed {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} card reward from defeating a [[Map Locations#Boss|Boss]] at the end of [[Acts|Act]] 1 and 2.\n* {{R|Dream Catcher}}'s card reward after resting at a [[Map Locations#Rest Sites|Rest Site]].\n* {{R|Tiny House}}'s card reward after acquiring it.\n* {{R|Prayer Wheel}}'s extra card reward from defeating [[Monsters|normal enemies]].\n* {{R|Orrery}}'s card rewards after acquiring it.\n* {{E|Sensory Stone}}'s 1-3 card rewards.\n\n=== Unaffected Card Rewards ===\n\nThe following card reward screens are '''not''' affected by {{R|Busted Crown}}:\n\n* {{C|Foreign Influence}}'s card reward when played.\n* {{C|Discovery}}'s card reward when played.\n* {{R|Toolbox}}'s card reward at the start of combat.\n* {{R|Nilry's Codex}}'s card reward at the end of each turn in combat.\n* {{P|Attack Potion}}, {{P|Skill Potion}}, and {{P|Power Potion}}'s card rewards when consumed.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* As with all {{KW|Energy}} relics, {{R|Busted Crown}} can allow the player to play high-impact expensive cards more easily.\n* The drawback of {{R|Busted Crown}} can be more manageable depending on the state of the player's run:\n** If the player is already confident in their deck and does not feel like many more cards are needed in order to win.\n** If the player has a large surplus of [[Gold]] (such as from {{R|Golden Idol}}, {{R|Membership Card}}, or {{E|Mind Bloom}}'s {{Frame|I am Rich}}), they can path to more [[Merchant|Merchants]] as their card offerings are not affected by {{R|Busted Crown}}.\n*** {{R|The Courier}} can restock the [[Merchant|Merchant's]] card offerings, potentially allowing the player to find many useful cards in the same shop.\n*** {{R|Wing Boots}} can help the player path to more [[Merchant|Merchants]] more easily.\n** If the player has other ways to find the cards they need, such as {{R|Nilry's Codex}} or {{C|Discovery}}+.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* The drawback of {{R|Busted Crown}} is lessened by {{R|Question Card}}.\n** The player effectively went from seeing 1 card in each card reward (thanks to {{R|Busted Crown}}'s debuff) to now seeing 2 cards in each card reward.\n* {{KW|Vintage}} drastically reduces the amount of card rewards the player will see, which provides even fewer opportunities for cards to be added to the player's deck.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{R|Dream Catcher}}, {{R|Prayer Wheel}}, {{R|Orrery}}, and {{R|Tiny House}} will all show 2 fewer cards in their card rewards.\n* Attempting to add cards to the player's deck from [[Slay the Spire Wiki/Enemies|enemy combat rewards]] becomes much less efficient due to the lower amount of cards presented.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* {{R|Busted Crown}} may be a reference to the item ''Cracked Crown'' from ''The Binding of Isaac: Rebirth''.<ref>https://bindingofisaacrebirth.wiki.gg/wiki/Cracked_Crown</ref>\n* The flavor text of {{R|Busted Crown}} suggests that it may have belonged to {{M|The Champ}}.\n** {{M|The Champ}} makes no direct comment or reference to the player possessing {{R|Busted Crown}} however, unlike when the player possesses {{R|Champion Belt}} which has a [[Champion Belt#Trivia|unique line of dialogue]] when entering {{M|The Champ}} fight.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 53: Blizzard'''\n** Busted Crown relic now flashes when its effect is triggered.\n* '''Weekly Patch 29: TURBO'''\n** We added special runs that you can play by entering specific seeds:\n** STARTERDECK Will give you Busted Crown and Binary (Meaning enemies drop 0 cards. Can you win with the starter deck??)\n* '''Weekly Patch 28: The Ritual'''\n** New Relic: Busted Crown\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"2316":{"pageid":2316,"ns":0,"title":"Calipers","revisions":[{"revid":56924,"parentid":50872,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Calipers\n|Image       = Calipers.png\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Description = At the start of your turn, lose 15 {{KW|Block}} rather than all of your {{KW|Block}}.\n|Flavor      = \"Mechanical precision leads to greatness\" - The Architect\n|InteractsWith = Block\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Block}}{{R|Calipers}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} [[Relic]].\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], by buying from the [[Merchant]], or found in a [[Medium Chest]] or [[Large Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Calling Bell}}, {{R|Shovel}}, and {{R|Black Star}}.\n** {{R|Calling Bell}}'s {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic can be {{R|Calipers}}.\n* Can be obtained from the following [[Events]]:\n** {{E|We Meet Again!}}: Can give {{R|Calipers}} in exchange for either a [[Potion]], some [[Gold]], or a [[Card]].\n** {{E|Wheel of Change}}: Can drop {{R|Calipers}} as a prize.\n** {{E|Big Fish}}: Can give {{R|Calipers}} along with {{C|Regret}}.\n** {{E|Dead Adventurer}}: Either by choosing {{Frame|Search}} and getting {{R|Calipers}} as a reward, or by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|Calipers}}).\n** {{E|Scrap Ooze}}: Can give {{R|Calipers}} with an X% chance, for increasing amounts of damage and likelihood of success on repeated attempts.\n** {{E|Pleading Vagrant}}: Can give {{R|Calipers}} in exchange for either 85 [[Gold]] by choosing {{Frame|Offer Gold}}, or {{C|Shame}} by choosing {{Frame|Rob}}.\n** {{E|The Colosseum}}: The {{Frame|VICTORY}} option drops 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic, and 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic (which can be {{R|Calipers}}).\n** {{E|The Mausoleum}}: Can give {{R|Calipers}} along with {{C|Writhe}}.\n** {{E|Mind Bloom}}: The {{Frame|I Am War}} option can drop {{R|Calipers}}.\n** {{E|Mysterious Sphere}}: The {{Frame|Open Sphere}} option can drop {{R|Calipers}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* The {{KW|Block}} gain penalty from {{C|Panic Button}} may be somewhat lessened if {{R|Calipers}} can help preserve some {{KW|Block}} between turns.\n* {{C|Entrench}} can help build up more {{KW|Block}} to be saved for future turns, and can also offset the 15 {{KW|Block}} loss from {{R|Calipers}} if the player has least 15 {{KW|Block}} before playing it.\n* Can enable {{C|Body Slam}} to do more damage through building up {{KW|Block}} over multiple turns.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Other {{KW|Block}}-preserving effects (namely {{C|Barricade}} and {{C|Blur}}) will take priority over {{R|Calipers}} and prevent the 15 {{KW|Block}} loss at the start of their turn.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Calipers (or callipers) are a tool used to measure the length, width, thickness, diameter, or depth of an object or hole.<ref>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calipers</ref> Its prongs are extended and retracted to clamp on an object (or until the tips line up with the edges of a hole) which can then be locked in place for measuring or applying directly to another workpiece.\n* There are many types of calipers, including:\n** ''Inside calipers '' for measuring internal dimensions of a hole.\n** ''Outside calipers'' for measuring the outer length/width/height/etc. of an object or hole.\n*** The {{R|Calipers}} relic are ''outside calipers''.\n** ''Oddleg calipers'' for drawing a line on a workpiece at a consistent distance.\n** ''Vernier calipers'', a modern style of calipers that can be used as inside or outside calipers, and have an LCD display to provide measurements directly on the tool itself.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!'''\n** Adding Relic: Calipers (was locked via char 3)\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"3031":{"pageid":3031,"ns":0,"title":"Circlet","revisions":[{"revid":51001,"parentid":37140,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Circlet\n|Image       = Circlet.png\n|Rarity      = Special\n|Description = Collect as many as you can.\n|Flavor      = You ran out of relics to find. Impressive!\n}}\n{{R|Circlet}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Special|Special}} [[Relic]] that is obtained once all other [[Relics]] have been collected. {{R|Circlet}} will stack in your relics list.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The {{R|Red Circlet}} is a relic meant to be obtained after all {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Boss|Boss Relics}} have been obtained but is unobtainable in the normal game due to a logic bug.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"1523":{"pageid":1523,"ns":0,"title":"Cracked Core","revisions":[{"revid":56349,"parentid":55710,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n| Name        = Cracked Core\n| Image       = CrackedCore.png\n| Rarity      = Starter\n| Character   = Defect\n| Description = At the start of each combat, {{KW|Channel}} 1 {{KW|Lightning}}.\n| Flavor      = The mysterious life force which powers the Automatons within the Spire. It appears to be cracked.\n| GivesToPlayer = Channel, Lightning\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Channel}}{{Keyword Infobox|Lightning}}\n{{R|Cracked Core}} is the {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Starter|Starter}} [[Relic]] of the [[Defect]]; they will always start every new run with it in their possession and it can't be obtained by any other character.\n\nIt can be upgraded into the {{R|Frozen Core}} {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Boss|Boss Relic}} if it's found in a Boss Chest.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* {{R|Cracked Core}}, {{R|Symbiotic Virus}}, and {{R|Nuclear Battery}} all {{KW|Channel}} an Orb at the start of combat. The order of these Orbs is determined by the order the Relics were acquired in. Since {{R|Cracked Core}} is always the first Relic acquired (assuming you still have it), the {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orb}} will always be '''Channelled''' first.\n** As there are only three Relics that '''Channel''' Orbs at the start of combat, and [[Defect]] always starts with at least three Orb Slots, the Orbs can never be {{KW|Evoke|Evoked}} before your first turn starts.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n==== a) General Orb Synergies ====\n* Other Orb sources, such as {{C|Darkness}} and {{C|Coolheaded}}, can be very helpful for {{KW|Evoke|Evoking}} {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orbs}} more frequently.\n* {{C|Thunder Strike}} hits more times for each {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orb}} {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} this combat, and {{C|Electrodynamics}} makes {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orbs}} hit all enemies.\n* Sources of {{BD|Focus}} will improve the effects of Orbs: {{C|Defragment}}, {{C|Consume}}, {{C|Biased Cognition}}, {{R|Data Disk}}\n* Sources of additional Orb Slots allow for having more [[Orbs#Passive|Orb Passives]] in parallel: {{C|Capacitor}}, {{R|Runic Capacitor}}, {{R|Inserter}}, {{P|Potion of Capacity}}\n* {{C|Bullseye}} applies {{BD|Lock-On}}, which makes damaging Orbs deal 50% more damage to that enemy.\n* {{C|Compile Driver}} draws a card for each unique type of Orb {{KW|Channel|Channeled}}.\n* {{C|Barrage}} deals damage for each {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} Orb, while {{C|Fission}} draws a card and adds 1 {{Icon|BE}} for each Channeled Orb.\n* {{C|Recursion}}, {{C|Dualcast}}, and {{C|Multi-Cast}} each can directly {{KW|Evoke}} your Orbs 1, 2, or X times respectively.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{C|Reprogram}} and {{C|Hyperbeam}} give negative {{BD|Focus}}, making {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orbs}} less effective.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** Content: 9 Relics.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"2121":{"pageid":2121,"ns":0,"title":"Inserter","revisions":[{"revid":55827,"parentid":55445,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Inserter\n|Image       = Inserter.png\n|Rarity      = Boss\n|Character   = Defect\n|Description = Every 2 turns, gain 1 {{KW|Orb}} slot.\n|Flavor      = Push. Pull. Stack. Repeat.\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Orb}}\n{{R|Inserter}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|character:Defect|Defect-exclusive}} {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Boss|Boss}} [[Relic]]. The counter that keeps track of how many turns have passed is not reset between combats, and it's incremented at the ''start'' of the player's turn. This means that if the counter is at 1 at the end of a combat, it will trigger at the start of the next combat and reset to 0 as normal.\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be obtained from [[Boss Swap]].\n* After fighting a [[Boss]], {{R|Inserter}} can be offered as a choice of 3 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Boss|Boss Relics}}.\n\n== Spawn Restrictions ==\n* Can only be obtained by [[Defect]].\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Order ===\n* {{R|Inserter}}'s counter is incremented at the start of the player's turn.\n* On turns where {{R|Inserter}} triggers, the {{KW|Orb}} Slot will be gained before the player draws their opening hand.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Barrage}} can deal a higher maximum damage with more {{KW|Orb}} Slots.\n* {{C|Fission}} can be used for more draw, {{Icon|BE}} [[Keywords#Energy|Energy]], and {{KW|Evoke|Evoked}} {{KW|Orb|Orbs}}.\n* {{C|Compile Driver}} draws an additional card for each different type of {{KW|Orb}} {{KW|Channel|Channeled}}; more {{KW|Orb}} Slots allows the maximum draw of 4 cards, as well as making it easier to keep multiple {{KW|Orb}} types {{KW|Channel|Channeled}}.\n* More {{KW|Orb}} Slots may benefit all {{KW|Orb}} generation sources, but especially ones which can fill slots quickly, such as {{C|Tempest}}, {{C|Chill}}, {{C|Glacier}}, {{C|Rainbow}}, and {{C|Electrodynamics}}.\n* {{C|Consume}} can be used more times with additional {{KW|Orb}} Slots, allowing for large {{BD|Focus}} gain.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* The maximum amount of {{KW|Orb}} Slots is 10.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* It has been confirmed by the Developers that {{R|Inserter}} is a reference to [https://wiki.factorio.com/Inserter Factorio's Inserter]. In particular, it is the standard, yellow inserter.\n* This relic still gives orb slots even to a character other than the [[Defect]], however this is impossible to actually occur in normal gameplay.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"2300":{"pageid":2300,"ns":0,"title":"Kunai","revisions":[{"revid":55834,"parentid":50846,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Kunai\n|Image       = Kunai.png\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Description = Every time you play 3 {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}} in a single turn, gain 1 {{BD|Dexterity}}\n|Flavor      = A blade favored by assassins for its lethality at range.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Dexterity}}{{R|Kunai}} is an {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} [[Relic]].\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], by buying from the [[Merchant]], or found in a [[Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Calling Bell}}, {{R|Shovel}}, {{R|Black Star}}, and {{R|Matryoshka}}.\n** {{R|Calling Bell}}'s {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic can be {{R|Kunai}}.\n** {{R|Matryoshka}}'s extra relic has a 25% chance of being {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}}, which can be {{R|Kunai}}.\n* Can be obtained from the following [[Events]]:\n** {{E|We Meet Again!}}: Can give {{R|Kunai}} in exchange for either a [[Potion]], some [[Gold]], or a [[Card]].\n** {{E|Wheel of Change}}: Can drop {{R|Kunai}} as a prize.\n** {{E|Big Fish}}: Can give {{R|Kunai}} along with {{C|Regret}}.\n** {{E|Dead Adventurer}}: Either by choosing {{Frame|Search}} and getting {{R|Kunai}} as a reward, or by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|Kunai}}).\n** {{E|Scrap Ooze}}: Can give {{R|Kunai}} with an X% chance, for increasing amounts of damage and likelihood of success on repeated attempts.\n** {{E|Pleading Vagrant}}: Can give {{R|Kunai}} in exchange for either 85 [[Gold]] by choosing {{Frame|Offer Gold}}, or {{C|Shame}} by choosing {{Frame|Rob}}.\n** {{E|The Colosseum}}: The {{Frame|VICTORY}} option drops 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic (which can be {{R|Kunai}}), and 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic.\n** {{E|The Mausoleum}}: Can give {{R|Kunai}} along with {{C|Writhe}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Works especially well with decks that generate many low-cost or zero-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}}:\n** [[Ironclad]] can combine {{C|Anger}}, {{C|Twin Strike}}, and {{C|Whirlwind}} for multiple {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}} per turn.\n** [[Silent]]'s {{C|Shiv}}-generating cards like {{C|Blade Dance}}, {{C|Cloak and Dagger}}, and {{C|Infinite Blades}} allow frequent triggering of {{R|Kunai}}.\n** [[Defect]] can utilize {{C|Claw}} and other cheap {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}} for repeated activations.\n** [[Watcher]] can use {{C|Flurry of Blows}} and other stance-based {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}} to reliably trigger it.\n* Works well with the other \"ninja relics\" which all interact with the number of {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}} played in some way:\n** {{R|Shuriken}} grants {{BD|Strength}} under similar conditions, complementing {{R|Kunai}}'s {{BD|Dexterity}}.\n** {{R|Nunchaku}} provides extra energy every 10 {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}}, supporting attack-heavy decks.\n** {{R|Ornamental Fan}} provides {{KW|Block}} for each trigger.\n** {{R|Ninja Scroll}} allows for an easy trigger at the start of every combat.\n\n=== Anti-Synergy ===\n* Decks that rely heavily on {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skills}} or {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Powers}} (e.g. block-focused [[Defect]] with {{KW|Frost|Frost Orbs}}, or [[Silent]] {{BD|Poison}} decks without {{C|Shiv|Shivs}}) may struggle to activate {{R|Kunai}} consistently.\n* When combined with effects that reduce card draw or limit playable cards (e.g. {{M|Time Eater}} or {{R|Velvet Choker}}), {{R|Kunai}}'s usefulness is diminished.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* {{R|Kunai}} is one of the relics in the \"ninja relics set\" which are all tools used in East-Asian Martial Arts and all synergize with a certain number of {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}} played; the others being {{R|Shuriken}}, {{R|Nunchaku}}, {{R|Ornamental Fan}}, and {{R|Ninja Scroll}}.\n** Honorable mention to {{R|Pen Nib}} which fits the ''mechanical'' theme of the ninja relics, but has no actual ''visual'' theming with ninjas or East-Asian Martial Arts.\n* Kunai are a traditional Japanese multipurpose tool and weapon; thought to be derived from masonry trowels. The visual design used in the game references the common pop culture portrayal, which is not accurate to traditional real-world kunai. A kunai is normally a small leaf-shaped blade and a handle with a ring on the end for attaching a rope.<ref>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kunai</ref>\n** Contrary to how they are often depicted in media and pop culture, they are traditionally a stabbing and slashing weapon and are not effective as thrown weaponry due to their weight and shape.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"2491":{"pageid":2491,"ns":0,"title":"Letter Opener","revisions":[{"revid":55837,"parentid":50847,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Letter Opener\n|Image       = LetterOpener.png\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Description = Every time you play 3 {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skills}} in a single turn, deal 5 damage to ALL enemies.\n|Flavor      = Unnaturally sharp.\n}}\n{{R|Letter Opener}} is an {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} [[Relic]]. Whenever 3 {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skills}} are played in the same turn, 5 damage is dealt to all enemies. This damage is not treated as {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} damage, and therefore does not benefit from effects like {{BD|Strength}}, {{BD|Vulnerable}}, or {{R|The Boot}}. {{R|Letter Opener}} can be triggered multiple times in the same turn, dealing its damage on the 3rd, 6th, 9th, etc. {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|skill}} played during the same turn.\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], by buying from the [[Merchant]], or found in a [[Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Calling Bell}}, {{R|Shovel}}, {{R|Black Star}}, and {{R|Matryoshka}}.\n** {{R|Calling Bell}}'s {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic can be {{R|Letter Opener}}.\n** {{R|Matryoshka}}'s extra relic has a 25% chance of being {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}}, which can be {{R|Letter Opener}}.\n* Can be obtained from the following [[Events]]:\n** {{E|We Meet Again!}}: Can give {{R|Letter Opener}} in exchange for either a [[Potion]], some [[Gold]], or a [[Card]].\n** {{E|Wheel of Change}}: Can drop {{R|Letter Opener}} as a prize.\n** {{E|Big Fish}}: Can give {{R|Letter Opener}} along with {{C|Regret}}.\n** {{E|Dead Adventurer}}: Either by choosing {{Frame|Search}} and getting {{R|Letter Opener}} as a reward, or by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|Letter Opener}}).\n** {{E|Scrap Ooze}}: Can give {{R|Letter Opener}} with an X% chance, for increasing amounts of damage and likelihood of success on repeated attempts.\n** {{E|Pleading Vagrant}}: Can give {{R|Letter Opener}} in exchange for either 85 [[Gold]] by choosing {{Frame|Offer Gold}}, or {{C|Shame}} by choosing {{Frame|Rob}}.\n** {{E|The Colosseum}}: The {{Frame|VICTORY}} option drops 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic (which can be {{R|Letter Opener}}), and 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic.\n** {{E|The Mausoleum}}: Can give {{R|Letter Opener}} along with {{C|Writhe}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Order ===\n* The effect(s) of the {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} that triggers {{R|Letter Opener}} will (usually* ) finish resolving before {{R|Letter Opener}} triggers its damage. This is somewhat deceptive, as {{R|Letter Opener}} will \"flash\" ''immediately'' when the skill is played.\n** E.g. If playing {{C|Defend (Ironclad)|Defend}} would trigger {{R|Letter Opener}}, the {{KW|Block}} is gained before {{R|Letter Opener}}'s damage triggers.\n** * In the case of cards like {{C|Havoc}} that play another card as its effect, {{R|Letter Opener}} will trigger after {{C|Havoc}} is discarded but before the card drawn by {{C|Havoc}} is played.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Letter Opener}} can provide a reliable source of damage for decks that otherwise lack direct damage through {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}}, or that must use all of their {{KW|Energy}} to focus on playing defensive-focused {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skills}} on turns where the enemy is attacking.\n* {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skills}} that fetch or create other skills can make it easier to trigger {{R|Letter Opener}} (such as {{C|Exhume}}, {{C|Burst}}, {{C|Hologram}}, and {{C|Scrawl}}).\n* Since {{R|Letter Opener}}'s damage is not {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} damage, it will not cause the player to take damage from {{BD|Thorns}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* {{C|Deus Ex Machina}} turning into {{C|Miracle|Miracles}} does not count as playing a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}}.\n* {{R|Letter Opener}}'s damage will not change {{M|Writhing Mass}}' intent.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* It can be difficult to make use of {{R|Letter Opener}} against {{M|Gremlin Nob}} as the enemy deals more damage for every {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} played.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* A letter opener (also called a \"paper knife\") is a semi-sharp blade used for cutting paper, such as the seams of paper envelopes.<ref>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paper_knife</ref>\n** Modern letter openers are typically not very sharp (except maybe at the very tip), hence the relic's flavor text \"''Unnaturally sharp.''\"\n* {{R|Letter Opener}} is one of the reasons why {{C|Exhume}} cannot target a 2nd copy of {{C|Exhume}} in the player's {{KW|Exhaust}} pile. It would be too easy to build an infinite damage combo using two copies of the upgraded {{C|Exhume}}+ to repeatedly trigger {{R|Letter Opener}} without needing to spend any {{KW|Energy}} or draw cards.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 13: Thinking Ahead'''\n** Fixed bug where Nemesis could take more than 1 damage from Thorns, Potions, and relics like Letter Opener.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"3120":{"pageid":3120,"ns":0,"title":"Lizard Tail","revisions":[{"revid":55842,"parentid":50885,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Lizard Tail\n|Image       = LizardTail.png\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Description = When you would die, heal to 50% of your Max HP instead (works once).\n|Flavor      = A fake tail to trick enemies during combat.\n}}\n{{R|Lizard Tail}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} [[Relic]].\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], by buying from the [[Merchant]], or found in a [[Medium Chest]] or [[Large Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Calling Bell}}, {{R|Shovel}}, and {{R|Black Star}}.\n** {{R|Calling Bell}}'s {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic can be {{R|Lizard Tail}}.\n* Can be obtained from the following [[Events]]:\n** {{E|We Meet Again!}}: Can give {{R|Lizard Tail}} in exchange for either a [[Potion]], some [[Gold]], or a [[Card]].\n** {{E|Wheel of Change}}: Can drop {{R|Lizard Tail}} as a prize.\n** {{E|Big Fish}}: Can give {{R|Lizard Tail}} along with {{C|Regret}}.\n** {{E|Dead Adventurer}}: Either by choosing {{Frame|Search}} and getting {{R|Lizard Tail}} as a reward, or by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|Lizard Tail}}).\n** {{E|Scrap Ooze}}: Can give {{R|Lizard Tail}} with an X% chance, for increasing amounts of damage and likelihood of success on repeated attempts.\n** {{E|Pleading Vagrant}}: Can give {{R|Lizard Tail}} in exchange for either 85 [[Gold]] by choosing {{Frame|Offer Gold}}, or {{C|Shame}} by choosing {{Frame|Rob}}.\n** {{E|The Colosseum}}: The {{Frame|VICTORY}} option drops 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic, and 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic (which can be {{R|Lizard Tail}}).\n** {{E|The Mausoleum}}: Can give {{R|Lizard Tail}} along with {{C|Writhe}}.\n** {{E|Mind Bloom}}: The {{Frame|I Am War}} option can drop {{R|Lizard Tail}}.\n** {{E|Mysterious Sphere}}: The {{Frame|Open Sphere}} option can drop {{R|Lizard Tail}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Order ===\n* Revival effects generally trigger from \"top to bottom\", so the potion {{P|Fairy in a Bottle}} will trigger before {{R|Lizard Tail}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* As with all healing effects, {{R|Lizard Tail}} restores no HP (and therefore fails to prevent the player's death) if the player possesses {{R|Mark of the Bloom}}.\n* Powerful multi-hit attacks from enemies can still kill the player through {{R|Lizard Tail}} by continuing to deal damage after the relic triggers its revival effect. For example, the {{M|Awakened One}}'s {{Int|Awakened One|Soul Strike}} or {{Int|Awakened One|Tackle}} attacks can be devastating and kill the player through several revival effects if they have been allowed to stack a lot of {{BD|Strength}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* {{R|Lizard Tail}} is a reference to how some lizards (such as certain species of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gecko geckos] and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skink skinks]) can shed their tail in a process called [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autotomy autotomy] to help them escape from predators.\n** This can help them narrowly avoid predators who catch their tail while the lizard runs away, leaving the predator occupied with the tail and the lizard can flee the encounter. Some lizards that can engage in autotomy can re-grow their lost tails after some time, although it is often imperfect afterwards.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n** Lizard Tail relic rarity changed from Boss -> Rare.\n* '''Weekly Patch 51: Recursion'''\n** Muzzle blight was applying twice to Lizard Tail and Fairy Potion.\n* '''Weekly Patch 32: Face Trader'''\n** Fixed Fairy Potion and Lizard Tail not triggering with Muzzle blight.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"3152":{"pageid":3152,"ns":0,"title":"Medical Kit","revisions":[{"revid":50964,"parentid":37200,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Medical Kit\n|Image       = MedicalKit.png\n|Rarity      = Shop\n|Description = {{KW|Unplayable}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}} cards can now be played. Whenever you play a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}} card, {{KW|Exhaust}} it.\n|Flavor      = \"Has everything you need! Anti-itch, anti-burn, anti-venom, and more!\"\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Unplayable}}{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}{{R|Medical Kit}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Shop|Shop}} [[Relic]]. {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}} cards can now be played and do not cost any {{KW|Energy}}.\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can only be bought from the [[Merchant]]. Only 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Shop|Shop Relic}} is available per [[Shop]], even with {{R|The Courier}}, since it cannot restock Shop Relics.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* The following {{KW|Exhaust}} synergy effects can effectively allow {{R|Medical Kit}} to turn {{KW|Unplayable}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Statuses}} into useful effects:\n** {{C|Feel No Pain}} grants 3 (4) {{KW|Block}}.\n** {{C|Dark Embrace}} will draw a card.\n** {{R|Dead Branch}} replaces the {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}} with a random playable cards.\n** {{R|Charon's Ashes}} deals 3 damage to all enemies.\n* {{R|Ink Bottle}} will increment its counter.\n** This is particularly useful since using {{R|Medical Kit}} to {{KW|Exhaust}} {{KW|Unplayable}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Statuses}} requires no {{KW|Energy}} to be spent.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{R|Strange Spoon}} can sometimes prevent the {{KW|Unplayable}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}} from {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausting}}, potentially causing the player to have to draw it again on a future turn.\n* {{C|Slimed}} is already playable so it gains no benefit from {{R|Medical Kit}}. The player will still have to spend 1 {{KW|Energy}} to {{KW|Exhaust}} it as normal.\n\n== Notes ==\n* {{R|Blue Candle}} is very similar to this relic but instead allows you to play {{KW|Unplayable}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curses}} in exchange for 1 HP each time.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Fixed certain Status and Curses triggering their end of turn effects by playing them normally with Medical Kit or Blue Candle under specific circumstances.\n* '''Weekly Patch 51: Recursion'''\n** Medical Kit relic will no longer cause Slimed cards to glow as if they could be played when you have no energy.\n** Medical Kit will no longer allow the player to sometimes play Slimed when out of energy.\n* '''Weekly Patch 40: Forethought'''\n** Blue Candle and Medical Kit wording changed to better reflect how they work with cards like Slimed.\n* '''Weekly Patch 10: Quality of Life'''\n** Fixed issue where Regret/Decay/Doubt/Burn fails to exhaust via Blue Candle and Medical Kit.\n* '''Weekly Patch 7: Setting Up All the Things'''\n** Blue Candle and Medical Kit should now work with Choke and Thousand Cuts.\n* '''Weekly Patch 3: Balance Balance Balance'''\n** Strange Spoon affects cards exhausted by Medical Kit and Blue Candle now.\n** After Image now works when playing Curse/Status cards via Medical Kit and Blue Candle.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"2563":{"pageid":2563,"ns":0,"title":"Molten Egg","revisions":[{"revid":55466,"parentid":50851,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Molten Egg\n|Image       = MoltenEgg2.png\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Description = Whenever you add an {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} card to your deck, {{KW|Upgrade}} it.\n|Flavor      = The egg of a Phoenix. It glows red hot with a simmering lava.\n|Keywords    = Deck\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Upgrade}}{{R|Molten Egg}} is an {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} [[Relic]].\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], by buying from the [[Merchant]], or found in a [[Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Calling Bell}}, {{R|Shovel}}, {{R|Black Star}}, and {{R|Matryoshka}}.\n** {{R|Calling Bell}}'s {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic can be {{R|Molten Egg}}.\n** {{R|Matryoshka}}'s extra relic has a 25% chance of being {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}}, which can be {{R|Molten Egg}}.\n* Can be obtained from the following [[Events]]:\n** {{E|We Meet Again!}}: Can give {{R|Molten Egg}} in exchange for either a [[Potion]], some [[Gold]], or a [[Card]].\n** {{E|Wheel of Change}}: Can drop {{R|Molten Egg}} as a prize.\n** {{E|Big Fish}}: Can give {{R|Molten Egg}} along with {{C|Regret}}.\n** {{E|Dead Adventurer}}: Either by choosing {{Frame|Search}} and getting {{R|Molten Egg}} as a reward, or by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|Molten Egg}}).\n** {{E|Scrap Ooze}}: Can give {{R|Molten Egg}} with an X% chance, for increasing amounts of damage and likelihood of success on repeated attempts.\n** {{E|Pleading Vagrant}}: Can give {{R|Molten Egg}} in exchange for either 85 [[Gold]] by choosing {{Frame|Offer Gold}}, or {{C|Shame}} by choosing {{Frame|Rob}}.\n** {{E|The Colosseum}}: The {{Frame|VICTORY}} option drops 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic (which can be {{R|Molten Egg}}), and 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic.\n** {{E|The Mausoleum}}: Can give {{R|Molten Egg}} along with {{C|Writhe}}.\n\n== Spawn Restrictions ==\nCan only be obtained below floor 49 (the last [[Rest Site]] before the [[Bosses#Act_3_Bosses|Act 3 Boss]]).\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Prayer Wheel}} and {{R|Question Card}} can provide more opportunities for the player to encounter {{KW|Upgrade|Upgraded}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}} from card rewards.\n* {{R|Molten Egg}} will automatically upgrade all {{C|Bite|Bites}} from the {{E|Vampires}} event.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}} created mid-combat (such as from {{R|Nilry's Codex}} which adds to the draw pile, or {{C|Infernal Blade}} which adds to the hand) will not be {{KW|Upgrade|Upgraded}} as {{R|Molten Egg}} only '''Upgrades''' card that are added to the player's '''deck'''.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* If the player has {{R|Snecko Eye}} and a way to upgrade cards mid-combat (such as {{C|Armaments}}), they will not be able to take advantage of reducing an {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack's}} {{KW|Energy}} cost if {{R|Snecko Eye}} makes it more expensive than its base cost.\n** For example, if {{R|Snecko Eye}} makes an un-{{KW|Upgrade|Upgraded}} {{C|Eruption}} cost 3 {{KW|Energy}}, '''Upgrading''' it will set its cost to 1 (the normal cost of {{C|Eruption}}+). But if it's already '''Upgraded''' in the player's deck from {{R|Molten Egg}}, this trick cannot be performed.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* {{R|Molten Egg}} is one of the relics in the \"egg relic set\" which {{KW|Upgrade}} cards of different types when added to the player's deck; the others being {{R|Toxic Egg}} for {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skills}} and {{R|Frozen Egg}} for {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Powers}}.\n* {{R|Molten Egg}} is called <code>Molten_Egg_2</code> internally as the egg relics were reworked in '''Weekly Patch 10: Quality of Life'''. These reworked versions ended up being the final version of the egg relics, so their modified internal name became their default internal name.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n** Egg relics now update card rewards in reward screens upon pickup.\n** Egg relics update card previews on Pandora's Box confirmation screen.\n** Fixed egg relics not upgrading card received from A Note To Yourself.\n* '''Weekly Patch 53: Blizzard'''\n** Fix for Egg relics causing an issue with cards in the Library event screen.\n* '''Weekly Patch 51: Recursion'''\n** Egg relics no longer spawn beyond floor 48 (excludes Endless mode).\n* '''Weekly Patch 40: Forethought'''\n** Gremlin Match and Keep event now has cards upgraded correctly.\n* '''Weekly Patch 32: Face Trader'''\n** Buying an egg relic in the shop will now correctly show cards in the shop upgraded.\n* '''Weekly Patch 31: Custom Mode'''\n** Match and Keep cards are now viewed as upgraded w/ Egg relics.\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** Egg relics now show pre-upgraded cards for Sensory Stone event's choices.\n* '''Weekly Patch 24: Potions?!'''\n** The three egg relics will now show the cards they are affecting as upgraded in card reward screens and shops.\n* '''Weekly Patch 13: Thinking Ahead'''\n** Egg relics (Toxic, Molten, Frozen) can now appear at Neow and some other scenarios.\n* '''Weekly Patch 10: Quality of Life'''\n** All 3 Egg relics (Molten/Toxic/Frozen) are now reworked. New eggs are Uncommon.\n** Molten Egg: Whenever you add an Attack card to your deck, it is Upgraded.\n* '''Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!'''\n** You can no longer cancel out of the selection screen for Egg relics.\n** Molten Egg is now Common (was Uncommon)\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"2591":{"pageid":2591,"ns":0,"title":"Mummified Hand","revisions":[{"revid":55865,"parentid":50852,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Mummified Hand\n|Image       = MummifiedHand.png\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Description = Whenever you play a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} card, a random card in your hand costs 0 that turn.\n|Flavor      = Frequently twitches, especially when your pulse is high.\n|Keywords    = Hand\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Energy}}{{R|Mummified Hand}} is an {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} [[Relic]]. The description is somewhat misleading, as the {{KW|Energy}}-reduction effect will be lost once played. Even if it's the same turn, if the affected card is played and then returned to the hand by any means (e.g. using {{C|Hologram}}), the card will be at its original cost.\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], by buying from the [[Merchant]], or found in a [[Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Calling Bell}}, {{R|Shovel}}, {{R|Black Star}}, and {{R|Matryoshka}}.\n** {{R|Calling Bell}}'s {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic can be {{R|Mummified Hand}}.\n** {{R|Matryoshka}}'s extra relic has a 25% chance of being {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}}, which can be {{R|Mummified Hand}}.\n* Can be obtained from the following [[Events]]:\n** {{E|We Meet Again!}}: Can give {{R|Mummified Hand}} in exchange for either a [[Potion]], some [[Gold]], or a [[Card]].\n** {{E|Wheel of Change}}: Can drop {{R|Mummified Hand}} as a prize.\n** {{E|Big Fish}}: Can give {{R|Mummified Hand}} along with {{C|Regret}}.\n** {{E|Dead Adventurer}}: Either by choosing {{Frame|Search}} and getting {{R|Mummified Hand}} as a reward, or by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|Mummified Hand}}).\n** {{E|Scrap Ooze}}: Can give {{R|Mummified Hand}} with an X% chance, for increasing amounts of damage and likelihood of success on repeated attempts.\n** {{E|Pleading Vagrant}}: Can give {{R|Mummified Hand}} in exchange for either 85 [[Gold]] by choosing {{Frame|Offer Gold}}, or {{C|Shame}} by choosing {{Frame|Rob}}.\n** {{E|The Colosseum}}: The {{Frame|VICTORY}} option drops 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic (which can be {{R|Mummified Hand}}), and 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic.\n** {{E|The Mausoleum}}: Can give {{R|Mummified Hand}} along with {{C|Writhe}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Order ===\n* {{R|Mummified Hand}} will trigger immediately after a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} is played, and before cards that interact with {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Powers}} being played (such as {{C|Heatsinks}} and {{C|Storm}}).\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* As with all randomly-targeted {{KW|Energy}}-reduction effects, {{R|Mummified Hand}}'s effect will never be \"wasted\" by targeting X-cost cards or any card which already costs 0 {{KW|Energy}} for any reason.\n* {{C|Creative AI}} can be used to generate a random {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} each turn to take advantage of {{R|Mummified Hand}} even when the player's deck has run out of other {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} cards.\n* Combining with {{C|Heatsinks}} makes all {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} cards become their own card draw and {{KW|Energy}} engine.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* Relying on {{R|Mummified Hand}} as the player's only source of additional {{KW|Energy}} can be dangerous when fighting {{M|Awakened One}} as playing {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Powers}} gives the boss additional {{BD|Strength}} for the rest of the fight.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Mummification is the process of preserving soft tissue by exposing it to [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Embalming embalming] chemicals or drying it out.<ref>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mummy</ref>\n** While mummification is most famously part of Ancient Egyptian history, mummies have been found in many parts of the world including historic sites in Southeast Asia, China, New Guinea, and Australia.\n* {{R|Mummified Hand}} only has 4 fingers, making it unlikely to have belonged to a human.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 50: The Final Act'''\n** Fix for Mummified Hand relic targeting cards with costs lowered by Setup or Forethought.\n* '''Weekly Patch 23: Testing Continues...'''\n** Streamline now correctly reduces cost even when its cost has been lowered to 0 for the turn by something like Mummified Hand.\n* '''Weekly Patch 21: Channel Lightning'''\n** Seeds are now utilized for Matryoshka and Mummified Hand relics.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"3121":{"pageid":3121,"ns":0,"title":"Old Coin","revisions":[{"revid":50887,"parentid":37217,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Old Coin\n|Image       = OldCoin.png\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Description = Upon pickup, gain 300 [[Gold]].\n|Flavor      = Unique coins are highly valued by Merchants for their historical value and rare metallic composition.\n}}\n{{R|Old Coin}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} [[Relic]]. Its only function is to give 300 [[Gold]] immediately on pickup.\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], or found in a [[Medium Chest]] or [[Large Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Calling Bell}}, {{R|Shovel}}, and {{R|Black Star}}.\n** {{R|Calling Bell}}'s {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic can be {{R|Old Coin}}.\n* Can be obtained from the following [[Events]]:\n** {{E|We Meet Again!}}: Can give {{R|Old Coin}} in exchange for either a [[Potion]], some [[Gold]], or a [[Card]].\n** {{E|Wheel of Change}}: Can drop {{R|Old Coin}} as a prize.\n** {{E|Big Fish}}: Can give {{R|Old Coin}} along with {{C|Regret}}.\n** {{E|Dead Adventurer}}: Either by choosing {{Frame|Search}} and getting {{R|Old Coin}} as a reward, or by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|Old Coin}}).\n** {{E|Scrap Ooze}}: Can give {{R|Old Coin}} with an X% chance, for increasing amounts of damage and likelihood of success on repeated attempts.\n** {{E|Pleading Vagrant}}: Can give {{R|Old Coin}} in exchange for either 85 [[Gold]] by choosing {{Frame|Offer Gold}}, or {{C|Shame}} by choosing {{Frame|Rob}}.\n** {{E|The Colosseum}}: The {{Frame|VICTORY}} option drops 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic, and 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic (which can be {{R|Old Coin}}).\n** {{E|The Mausoleum}}: Can give {{R|Old Coin}} along with {{C|Writhe}}.\n** {{E|Mind Bloom}}: The {{Frame|I Am War}} option can drop {{R|Old Coin}}.\n** {{E|Mysterious Sphere}}: The {{Frame|Open Sphere}} option can drop {{R|Old Coin}}.\n\n== Spawn Restrictions ==\n* Can only be obtained below floor 49 (the last [[Rest Site]] before the [[Bosses#Act_3_Bosses|Act 3 Boss]]).\n* Cannot be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Triggers {{R|Bloody Idol}} on pickup.\n* If {{R|Old Coin}} is removed by {{E|N'loth}}, the player will not lose any [[Gold]].\n* The purchasing power (or \"effective gold\") at [[Merchant|Shops]] granted by {{R|Old Coin}} increases if the player has {{R|The Courier}} and/or {{R|Membership Card}}.\n<!--\nBe very careful with the math if you decide rewrite this section.\nThe correct formula for purchasing power (or \"effective gold\") is [  300 / (1 - discount)  ] and NOT [  300 * (1 + discount)  ].\nA 50% discount should DOUBLE the purchasing power (+100%)! It's not just a 50% increase.\n-->\n** {{R|The Courier|The Courier's}} 20% discount makes the 300 [[Gold]] from {{R|Old Coin}} have the purchasing power of 375 [[Gold]].\n** {{R|Membership Card|Membership Card's}} 50% discount makes the 300 [[Gold]] from {{R|Old Coin}} have the purchasing power of 600 [[Gold]].\n** Having both {{R|The Courier}} and {{R|Membership Card}} is a total 60% discount. This makes the 300 [[Gold]] from {{R|Old Coin}} have the purchasing power of 750 [[Gold]].\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* If {{R|Old Coin}} is removed by {{E|N'loth}}, the player will not lose any [[Gold]].\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{R|Ectoplasm}}, if acquired first, renders {{R|Old Coin}} useless.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* {{R|Old Coin}} was used to model the collectible metal coins that come with the Collector's Edition of ''Slay the Spire: The Board Game''.<ref>https://contentiongames.myshopify.com/products/slay-the-spire-the-board-game-collectors-edition</ref><ref>https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/contentiongames/slay-the-spire-the-board-game/description</ref>\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 51: Recursion'''\n** Old Coin relic no longer spawns beyond floor 48 (excludes Endless mode).\n* '''Weekly Patch 25: Building Blocks'''\n** Cauldron and Old Coin wording improved to match other relics.\n* '''Weekly Patch 3: Balance Balance Balance'''\n** Old Coin relic buffed.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"3149":{"pageid":3149,"ns":0,"title":"Orrery","revisions":[{"revid":50968,"parentid":37222,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Orrery\n|Image       = Orrery.png\n|Rarity      = Shop\n|Description = Upon pickup, choose and add 5 cards to your deck.\n|Flavor      = \"Once you understand the universe...\" - Zoroth\n|Keywords    = Deck\n}}\n{{R|Orrery}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Shop|Shop}} [[Relic]]. It presents the player with 5 normal card rewards on pickup.\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can only be bought from the [[Merchant]]. Only 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Shop|Shop Relic}} is available per [[Shop]], even with {{R|The Courier}}, since it cannot restock Shop Relics.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Question Card}} will present the player with 1 additional card to choose from in each of the 5 card rewards.\n* {{R|Singing Bowl}} can be used to skip any of the 5 card rewards, granting +2 Max HP for each reward skipped in this way. A total of 10 Max HP if all card rewards are skipped.\n* {{R|Molten Egg}}, {{R|Toxic Egg}}, and {{R|Frozen Egg}} will cause any {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}}, {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skills}}, and {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Powers}} (respectively) to be {{KW|Upgrade|upgraded}}.\n* {{R|N'loth's Gift}} will increase the likelihood of {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare cards}} being offered. For more information on rare card chance, see [[Cards#Card_Distribution|Card Distribution]].\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{R|Busted Crown}} will present the player with 2 fewer cards to choose from in each of the 5 card rewards.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* An orrery is a mechanical model of the solar system. It is used in classical astronomy to predict the relative positions and orbital motions of planets and moons.<ref>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orrery</ref>\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n** Orrery relic rarity changed from Boss -> Shop.\n* '''Weekly Patch 4: Full speed ahead!'''\n** Orrery is a boss relic again.\n* '''Weekly Patch 3: Balance Balance Balance'''\n** HOTFIX: Orrery is temporarily removed because it crashes.\n** Orrery is now an uncommon relic.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"2592":{"pageid":2592,"ns":0,"title":"Pantograph","revisions":[{"revid":55887,"parentid":50854,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Pantograph\n|Image       = Pantograph.png\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Description = At the start of Boss combats, heal 25 HP.\n|Flavor      = \"Solid foundations are not accidental. Tools for planning are a must.\" - The Architect\n}}\n{{R|Pantograph}} is an {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} [[Relic]].\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], by buying from the [[Merchant]], or found in a [[Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Calling Bell}}, {{R|Shovel}}, {{R|Black Star}}, and {{R|Matryoshka}}.\n** {{R|Calling Bell}}'s {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic can be {{R|Pantograph}}.\n** {{R|Matryoshka}}'s extra relic has a 25% chance of being {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}}, which can be {{R|Pantograph}}.\n* Can be obtained from the following [[Events]]:\n** {{E|We Meet Again!}}: Can give {{R|Pantograph}} in exchange for either a [[Potion]], some [[Gold]], or a [[Card]].\n** {{E|Wheel of Change}}: Can drop {{R|Pantograph}} as a prize.\n** {{E|Big Fish}}: Can give {{R|Pantograph}} along with {{C|Regret}}.\n** {{E|Dead Adventurer}}: Either by choosing {{Frame|Search}} and getting {{R|Pantograph}} as a reward, or by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|Pantograph}}).\n** {{E|Scrap Ooze}}: Can give {{R|Pantograph}} with an X% chance, for increasing amounts of damage and likelihood of success on repeated attempts.\n** {{E|Pleading Vagrant}}: Can give {{R|Pantograph}} in exchange for either 85 [[Gold]] by choosing {{Frame|Offer Gold}}, or {{C|Shame}} by choosing {{Frame|Rob}}.\n** {{E|The Colosseum}}: The {{Frame|VICTORY}} option drops 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic (which can be {{R|Pantograph}}), and 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic.\n** {{E|The Mausoleum}}: Can give {{R|Pantograph}} along with {{C|Writhe}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Pantograph}}'s healing occurs during combat. This allows it to benefit from the healing bonus from {{R|Magic Flower}}, healing 38 HP instead of 25.\n* {{R|Pantograph}} will trigger its healing on the bonus [[Boss]] fight from the {{E|Mind Bloom}} event, and {{Asc|20|both of the Act 3 bosses}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* As with all healing effects, {{R|Pantograph}} restores no HP if the player possesses {{R|Mark of the Bloom}}.\n* {{R|Pantograph}}'s healing can disable {{R|Red Skull}} right at the start of a [[Boss]] fight when the player may want its {{BD|Strength}} bonus the most.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* A pantograph is a mechanical device that was historically used to accurately trace existing drawings into another copy, often allowing for a relatively simple way to reproduce the original in a larger size without loss of detail.<ref>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pantograph</ref> Modern versions of a pantograph can use a milling machine to allow for replication of wood, stone, or metal designs.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 37: Darkness'''\n** Red Skull relic no longer has odd behavior if you heal at the start of combat (Pantograph, etc).\n* '''Weekly Patch 4: Full speed ahead!'''\n** Pantograph no longer heals double on Donu and Deca boss.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"1441":{"pageid":1441,"ns":0,"title":"Paper Phrog","revisions":[{"revid":56327,"parentid":55890,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n| Name        = Paper Phrog\n| Image       = PaperFrog.png\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Character   = Ironclad\n| Description = Enemies with {{BD|Vulnerable}} take 75% more damage rather than 50%.\n| Flavor      = The paper continually folds and unfolds itself into the shape of a small creature.\n| InteractsWith = Exhaust\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Vulnerable}}\n{{R|Paper Phrog}} is an {{QueryLink|Relics|character:Ironclad|Ironclad-exclusive}} {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} [[Relic]]. It further increases the damage bonus from {{BD|Vulnerable}} from 50% to 75%; multiplying the damage from each {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} by 1.75. As usual, the final total damage is always rounded down.\n\nTargeting a {{BD|Vulnerable}} enemy with an {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} will always show the correct damage number. For example, an un-buffed {{C|Strike (Ironclad)|Strike}} will show 10 damage instead of the usual 9 if the player did not possess {{R|Paper Phrog}}.\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], by buying from the [[Merchant]], or found in a [[Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Calling Bell}}, {{R|Shovel}}, {{R|Black Star}}, and {{R|Matryoshka}}.\n** {{R|Calling Bell}}'s {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic can be {{R|Paper Phrog}}.\n** {{R|Matryoshka}}'s extra relic has a 25% chance of being {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}}, which can be {{R|Paper Phrog}}.\n* Can be obtained from the following [[Events]]:\n** {{E|We Meet Again!}}: Can give {{R|Paper Phrog}} in exchange for either a [[Potion]], some [[Gold]], or a [[Card]].\n** {{E|Wheel of Change}}: Can drop {{R|Paper Phrog}} as a prize.\n** {{E|Big Fish}}: Can give {{R|Paper Phrog}} along with {{C|Regret}}.\n** {{E|Dead Adventurer}}: Either by choosing {{Frame|Search}} and getting {{R|Paper Phrog}} as a reward, or by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|Paper Phrog}}).\n** {{E|Scrap Ooze}}: Can give {{R|Paper Phrog}} with an X% chance, for increasing amounts of damage and likelihood of success on repeated attempts.\n** {{E|Pleading Vagrant}}: Can give {{R|Paper Phrog}} in exchange for either 85 [[Gold]] by choosing {{Frame|Offer Gold}}, or {{C|Shame}} by choosing {{Frame|Rob}}.\n** {{E|The Colosseum}}: The {{Frame|VICTORY}} option drops 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic (which can be {{R|Paper Phrog}}), and 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic.\n** {{E|The Mausoleum}}: Can give {{R|Paper Phrog}} along with {{C|Writhe}}.\n\n== Spawn Restrictions ==\n* Can only be obtained by [[Ironclad]].\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Synergies ===\nAnything that applies {{BD|Vulnerable}} to enemies will be more effective with {{R|Paper Phrog}}:\n\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Bash}}\n* {{C|Thunderclap}}\n* {{C|Shockwave}}\n* {{C|Uppercut}}\n* {{C|Trip}}\n\nThe following cards can benefit from {{R|Paper Phrog}} if acquired from another character's card pool, such as via {{R|Prismatic Shard}}:\n\n* {{C|Terror}}\n* {{C|Beam Cell}}\n* {{C|Crush Joints}}\n* {{C|Indignation}}\n\n==== Relics ====\n* {{R|Bag of Marbles}}\n* {{R|Champion Belt}}, although it doesn't directly affect the {{BD|Vulnerable}}.\n* {{R|Hand Drill}}\n\n==== Potions ====\n* {{P|Fear Potion}}\n\n== Trivia ==\n* {{R|Paper Phrog}}, just like {{R|Paper Krane}}, is an example of ''Origami''; the Japanese art of folding paper into recognizable objects.<ref>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Origami</ref>\n* It is not known why the relic's name is spelled ''Phrog'' instead of the correct spelling of ''Frog''.\n* Internally called <code>Paper Frog</code>.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"2593":{"pageid":2593,"ns":0,"title":"Question Card","revisions":[{"revid":55482,"parentid":50856,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Question Card\n|Image       = QuestionCard.png\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Description = Future card rewards have 1 additional card to choose from.\n|Flavor      = \"Those with more choices minimize the downside to chaos.\" - Kublai the Great\n}}\n{{R|Question Card}} is an {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} [[Relic]].\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], by buying from the [[Merchant]], or found in a [[Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Calling Bell}}, {{R|Shovel}}, {{R|Black Star}}, and {{R|Matryoshka}}.\n** {{R|Calling Bell}}'s {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic can be {{R|Question Card}}.\n** {{R|Matryoshka}}'s extra relic has a 25% chance of being {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}}, which can be {{R|Question Card}}.\n* Can be obtained from the following [[Events]]:\n** {{E|We Meet Again!}}: Can give {{R|Question Card}} in exchange for either a [[Potion]], some [[Gold]], or a [[Card]].\n** {{E|Wheel of Change}}: Can drop {{R|Question Card}} as a prize.\n** {{E|Big Fish}}: Can give {{R|Question Card}} along with {{C|Regret}}.\n** {{E|Dead Adventurer}}: Either by choosing {{Frame|Search}} and getting {{R|Question Card}} as a reward, or by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|Question Card}}).\n** {{E|Scrap Ooze}}: Can give {{R|Question Card}} with an X% chance, for increasing amounts of damage and likelihood of success on repeated attempts.\n** {{E|Pleading Vagrant}}: Can give {{R|Question Card}} in exchange for either 85 [[Gold]] by choosing {{Frame|Offer Gold}}, or {{C|Shame}} by choosing {{Frame|Rob}}.\n** {{E|The Colosseum}}: The {{Frame|VICTORY}} option drops 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic (which can be {{R|Question Card}}), and 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic.\n** {{E|The Mausoleum}}: Can give {{R|Question Card}} along with {{C|Writhe}}.\n\n== Spawn Restrictions ==\nCan only be obtained below floor 49 (the last [[Rest Site]] before the [[Bosses#Act_3_Bosses|Act 3 Boss]]).\n\n== Interactions ==\n\nOnly card rewards that would permanently add a card to the player's deck are affected by {{R|Question Card}}. Effects will generally mention ''\"obtain a card\"'' or specifically adding a card ''\"to your deck\"'' when they acts as card rewards, while effects that '''don't''' act as card rewards will always be phrased like ''\"choose 1 of 3 cards\"'' while in combat.\n\nFor completeness, all scenarios that seem like they could be considered a card reward during normal gameplay are listed in the sections below depending on whether they are affected by {{R|Question Card}} or not.\n\n=== Affected Card Rewards ===\n\nThe following card reward screens are affected by {{R|Question Card}} and will show 1 additional card to choose from:\n\n* End-of-combat card rewards from defeating [[Monsters|normal enemies]].\n* End-of-combat card rewards from defeating [[Elites|elites]].\n* The guaranteed {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} card reward from defeating a [[Map Locations#Boss|Boss]] at the end of [[Acts|Act]] 1 and 2.\n* {{R|Dream Catcher}}'s card reward after resting at a [[Map Locations#Rest Sites|Rest Site]].\n* {{R|Tiny House}}'s card reward after acquiring it.\n* {{R|Prayer Wheel}}'s extra card reward from defeating [[Monsters|normal enemies]].\n* {{R|Orrery}}'s card rewards after acquiring it.\n* {{E|Sensory Stone}}'s 1-3 card rewards.\n\n=== Unaffected Card Rewards ===\n\nThe following card reward screens are '''not''' affected by {{R|Question Card}}:\n\n* {{C|Foreign Influence}}'s card reward when played.\n* {{C|Discovery}}'s card reward when played.\n* {{R|Toolbox}}'s card reward at the start of combat.\n* {{R|Nilry's Codex}}'s card reward at the end of each turn in combat.\n* {{P|Attack Potion}}, {{P|Skill Potion}}, and {{P|Power Potion}}'s card rewards when consumed.\n* If {{R|Question Card}} was dropped by an [[Elite]], the card reward dropped by that same [[Elite]] will not benefit from {{R|Question Card}}.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Dream Catcher}}, {{R|Prayer Wheel}}, {{R|Orrery}}, and {{R|Tiny House}} will all show 1 additional card in their card rewards.\n* {{R|Molten Egg}}, {{R|Toxic Egg}}, and {{R|Frozen Egg}} will still upgrade the additional card if it's added to the player's deck.\n* {{R|N'loth's Gift}} can show slightly more {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} cards since overall more cards are shown. For more information on rare card chance, see [[Cards#Card Distribution|Card Distribution]].\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Lessens the drawback from {{R|Busted Crown}}.\n** The player effectively went from seeing 1 card in each card reward (thanks to '''Busted Crown''''s debuff) to now seeing 2 cards in each card reward.\n* {{KW|Vintage}} drastically reduces the amount of card rewards the player will see, which provides less opportunities for {{R|Question Card}} to trigger but also helps show the player more cards than if they did not have {{R|Question Card}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Likely a reference to the items ''Options?''<ref>https://bindingofisaacrebirth.wiki.gg/wiki/Options%3F</ref>, ''There's Options''<ref>https://bindingofisaacrebirth.wiki.gg/wiki/There%27s_Options</ref>, and potentially ''More Options''<ref>https://bindingofisaacrebirth.wiki.gg/wiki/More_Options</ref> from [https://bindingofisaacrebirth.wiki.gg/ The Binding of Isaac: Rebirth] due to their similar visual designs and effects.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 51: Recursion'''\n** Question Card relic no longer spawns beyond floor 48 (excludes Endless mode).\n* '''Weekly Patch 28: The Ritual'''\n** Removing non-keyword gold text on Question Card relic description.\n* '''Weekly Patch 21: Channel Lightning'''\n** Question Card indicates it works on future card rewards as it's no longer a boss relic.\n* '''Weekly Patch 18: Paranormal'''\n** Question Card relic is now Uncommon. (was Boss).\n* '''Weekly Patch 15: Surprise Patch'''\n** Question Card wording now accurately reflects what it does when accounting for other effects like Binary.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"2568":{"pageid":2568,"ns":0,"title":"Sacred Bark","revisions":[{"revid":50932,"parentid":37250,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Sacred Bark\n|Image       = SacredBark.png\n|Rarity      = Boss\n|Description = Double the effectiveness of [[Potions|potions]].\n|Flavor      = A bark rumored to originate from the World tree.\n}}\n{{R|Sacred Bark}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Boss|Boss}} [[Relic]] that doubles the effects of most [[Potions]].\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be obtained from [[Boss Swap]].\n* After fighting a [[Boss]], {{R|Sacred Bark}} can be offered as a choice of 3 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Boss|Boss Relics}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Alchemize}} can allow the player to gain an extra [[Potions|Potion]] each combat.\n* {{R|White Beast Statue}} guarantees that every combat will drop a [[Potions|Potion]] as a reward.\n* {{R|Potion Belt}} allows the player to hold on to more [[Potions]] at the same time.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{R|Sozu}} prevents the player from acquiring any more [[Potions]], so they will be stuck with whatever [[Potions]] they currently have for the rest of the run. This means, at best, {{R|Sacred Bark}} will only be able to affect 3 ({{Asc|11|2}}) [[Potions]], or 5 ({{Asc|11|4}}) with {{R|Potion Belt}}, for the rest of the run.\n\n=== Affected Potions ===\nTo see a full list of [[Potions]] and their effects, including {{R|Sacred Bark}}'s changes, see [[Potions List]].\n\n=== Unaffected Potions ===\n{{R|Sacred Bark}} has no effect the following [[Potions]] as there is no way to reasonably \"double\" their effect:\n* {{P|Ambrosia}}\n* {{P|Blessing of the Forge}}\n* {{P|Entropic Brew}}\n* {{P|Elixir}}\n* {{P|Gambler's Brew}}\n* {{P|Smoke Bomb}}\n* {{P|Stance Potion}}\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"2107":{"pageid":2107,"ns":0,"title":"Symbiotic Virus","revisions":[{"revid":55968,"parentid":55505,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}} \n{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Symbiotic Virus\n|Image       = SymbioticVirus.png\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Character   = Defect\n|Description = At the start of each combat, {{KW|Channel}} 1 {{KW|Dark}}.\n|Flavor      = A little bit of bad can do a lot of good.\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Channel}} {{Keyword Infobox|Dark}}\n{{R|Symbiotic Virus}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|character:Defect|Defect-exclusive}} {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} [[Relic]].\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], by buying from the [[Merchant]], or found in a [[Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Calling Bell}}, {{R|Shovel}}, {{R|Black Star}}, and {{R|Matryoshka}}.\n** {{R|Calling Bell}}'s {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic can be {{R|Symbiotic Virus}}.\n** {{R|Matryoshka}}'s extra relic has a 25% chance of being {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}}, which can be {{R|Symbiotic Virus}}.\n* Can be obtained from the following [[Events]]:\n** {{E|We Meet Again!}}: Can give {{R|Symbiotic Virus}} in exchange for either a [[Potion]], some [[Gold]], or a [[Card]].\n** {{E|Wheel of Change}}: Can drop {{R|Symbiotic Virus}} as a prize.\n** {{E|Big Fish}}: Can give {{R|Symbiotic Virus}} along with {{C|Regret}}.\n** {{E|Dead Adventurer}}: Either by choosing {{Frame|Search}} and getting {{R|Symbiotic Virus}} as a reward, or by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|Symbiotic Virus}}).\n** {{E|Scrap Ooze}}: Can give {{R|Symbiotic Virus}} with an X% chance, for increasing amounts of damage and likelihood of success on repeated attempts.\n** {{E|Pleading Vagrant}}: Can give {{R|Symbiotic Virus}} in exchange for either 85 [[Gold]] by choosing {{Frame|Offer Gold}}, or {{C|Shame}} by choosing {{Frame|Rob}}.\n** {{E|The Colosseum}}: The {{Frame|VICTORY}} option drops 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic (which can be {{R|Symbiotic Virus}}), and 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic.\n** {{E|The Mausoleum}}: Can give {{R|Symbiotic Virus}} along with {{C|Writhe}}.\n\n== Spawn Restrictions ==\nCan only be obtained by [[Defect]].\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* {{R|Symbiotic Virus}}, {{R|Cracked Core}}, and {{R|Nuclear Battery}} all {{KW|Channel}} an [[Orb]] at the start of combat. The order of these Orbs is determined by the order the relics were acquired in. Since {{R|Cracked Core}} is always the first relic acquired (assuming you still have it), the {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orb}} will always be {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} first.\n** As there are only three relics that {{KW|Channel}} [[Orbs]] at the start of combat, and [[Defect]] always starts with at least three Orb slots, the Orbs can never be {{KW|Evoke|Evoked}} before your first turn starts.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n==== a) General Orb Synergies ====\n* Other Orb sources, such as {{C|Ball Lightning}} and {{C|Coolheaded}}, can be very helpful for {{KW|Evoke|Evoking}} {{KW|Dark|Dark Orbs}} more frequently.\n* {{C|Darkness|Darkness+}} will trigger the [[Orbs#Passive|Passives]] of all {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} {{KW|Dark|Dark Orbs}}.\n* Sources of {{BD|Focus}} will improve the effects of Orbs: {{C|Defragment}}, {{C|Consume}}, {{C|Biased Cognition}}, {{R|Data Disk}}\n* Sources of additional Orb Slots allow for having more Orb [[Orbs#Passive|Passives]] in parallel: {{C|Capacitor}}, {{R|Runic Capacitor}}, {{R|Inserter}}, {{P|Potion of Capacity}}\n* {{C|Bullseye}} applies {{BD|Lock-On}}, which makes damaging Orbs deal 50% more damage to that enemy.\n* {{C|Compile Driver}} draws a card for each unique type of Orb {{KW|Channel|Channeled}}.\n* {{C|Barrage}} deals damage for each {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} Orb, while {{C|Fission}} draws a card and adds 1 {{Icon|BE}} for each Channeled Orb.\n* {{C|Recursion}}, {{C|Dualcast}}, and {{C|Multi-Cast}} each can directly {{KW|Evoke}} your Orbs 1, 2, or X times respectively.\n** {{C|Recursion}} in particular will keep the current damage value of an {{KW|Evoke|Evoked}} {{KW|Dark|Dark Orb}}, allowing it to continue growing and deal even more damage the next time it's {{KW|Evoke|Evoked}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{C|Reprogram}} and {{C|Hyperbeam}} give negative {{BD|Focus}}, making {{KW|Dark|Dark Orbs}} scale their damage more slowly.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"2542":{"pageid":2542,"ns":0,"title":"Whetstone","revisions":[{"revid":50831,"parentid":37292,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Whetstone\n|Image       = Whetstone.png\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Description = Upon pickup, {{KW|Upgrade}} 2 random {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}}.\n|Flavor      = \"Flesh never beats steel.\" - Kublai the Great\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Upgrade}}{{R|Whetstone}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Common|Common}} [[Relic]].\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], by buying from the [[Merchant]], or found in a [[Small Chest]] or [[Medium Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Shovel}}, {{R|Black Star}}, and {{R|Matryoshka}}.\n** {{R|Matryoshka}}'s extra relic has a 75% chance of being {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Common|Common}}, which can be {{R|Whetstone}}.\n* Can be obtained from the {{E|Dead Adventurer}} [[Event]] by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|Whetstone}}).\n* Can be obtained from the {{E|Wheel of Change}} [[Event]] by earning {{R|Whetstone}} as a prize.\n\n== Spawn Restrictions ==\nCannot be obtained from {{R|Calling Bell}} and \"Obtain Relic\" events that drop the relic without it being a combat reward. This means, for example, {{R|Whetstone}} can be obtained from {{E|Dead Adventurer}} if the [[Elite]] is beaten, but cannot be obtained from the {{Frame|Search}} option.\n\n== Interactions ==\n* {{R|Whetstone}} can be removed by {{E|N'loth}} with no penalty to the player's cards that were upgraded by the relic.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Unlike {{R|Bottled Flame}}, {{R|Whetstone}} ''can'' drop even if the player has no {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|attacks}} in their deck.\n* {{R|Whetstone}} can still drop even if all the '''attacks''' in the player's deck have already been {{KW|Upgrade|upgraded}}.\n* Despite working in a similar way to {{R|War Paint}}, {{R|War Paint}} does not share {{R|Whetstone}}'s [[#Spawn Restrictions|spawning restriction]] of being unable to be acquired from \"Obtain Relic\" events.\n** E.g. {{R|Whetstone}} can't be acquired from the {{Frame|Search}} option in the {{E|Dead Adventurer}} event and as a reward from {{R|Calling Bell}}, while {{R|War Paint}} can.\n* The flavor text may be a possible reference to the popular [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Role-playing_video_game CRPG] ''PlaneScape Torment'''s \"Second Cirle of Zerthimon\".<ref>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Planescape:_Torment</ref> An in-game religious text can be found quoting a historic slave race leader as saying: \"* Know* that flesh cannot mark steel. * Know* that steel may mark flesh. In * knowing* this, Zerthimon became free.\", as one of its core tenants.<ref>https://torment.fandom.com/wiki/Unbroken_Circle_of_Zerthimon#Second_Circle_of_Zerthimon</ref>\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 51: Recursion'''\n** Updated relic art for Whetstone.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]}}}}